; trentpower.fr — server-side PHP auto_prepend (TEMPLATE, not deployed by build).
;
; Why this lives in tools/server/ and NOT in public/:
;   This file references an absolute server path
;   (/srv/data/web/vhosts/...) which is meaningful only on the Gandi
;   instance. Committing it under public/ would (a) leak that path
;   into git and (b) require .htaccess to keep it 403'd. The build
;   gate now refuses to ship any .user.ini under public/.
;
; Operational state on the live host:
;   The server keeps its own .user.ini at
;   /vhosts/trentpower.fr/htdocs/.user.ini. The local lftp deploy and
;   the GitHub workflow both run `mirror -R` WITHOUT --delete, so the
;   server-side file is left in place across deploys. This template
;   exists so the directive is recoverable from version control.
;
; If the server file is ever lost, redeploy by hand:
;   sftp ...@sftp.sd3.gpaas.net
;   cd /vhosts/trentpower.fr/htdocs
;   put tools/server/user.ini.example .user.ini
;
; .htaccess in public/ already denies HTTP access to .user.ini at the
; Apache layer (Files + FilesMatch rules), so even if the file is
; uploaded, it cannot be read over the web.

auto_prepend_file = /srv/data/web/vhosts/trentpower.fr/htdocs/private/access-logger.php
